`runCatching` catches `CancellationException` as well, so a cancellation of this `viewModelScope` coroutine while `primeSession()` is suspended (e.g. the ViewModel is cleared mid-startup) is swallowed and logged as a failure instead of propagating, and the code continues into `_state.update` and `collect`. Prefer an explicit catch that rethrows cancellation:

```kotlin
try {
    userSessionRepository.primeSession()
} catch (e: CancellationException) {
    throw e
} catch (e: Exception) {
    Logger.w(e) { "Session prime failed; continuing without it" }
}
```

(`kotlin.coroutines.cancellation.CancellationException` is the common-code type to import here.)

